This is a fundamentally different kind of agent from ALA/EIP/ESS/HSI/BRA/RDA: it is a **scheduled batch process, not a per-record webhook-triggered agent.** It runs once daily and processes a backlog, rather than firing once per review.

=== KEY CONTEXT FROM v2.0 (confirmed accurate, carry forward) ===
- Six clients: PAK-001 (Park Avenue Kitchen), AJI-001 through AJI-005 (five Aji Ceviche Bar locations).
- Triggers daily at 5am UTC.
- Fetches pending records from RDA's NocoDB table, resolves each to its destination Google Sheet via a Client Config table, deduplicates against existing sheet rows, appends via the Google Sheets API using Service Account auth.
- Service Account auth (not OAuth2) was a deliberate choice — OAuth2 refresh tokens don't survive reliably in scheduled/task-runner execution mode.
- SplitInBatches is used specifically to force single-item processing through dynamic sheet resolution, because the native Google Sheets node only evaluates document/sheet ID expressions once per batch — a real, documented n8n limitation being worked around, not a stylistic choice.
- v2.0 fixed seven production defects found during live Aji pilot onboarding; three are named explicitly: line-break normalization for Spanish drafts (matches an exact code comment found in the live workflow), switching NocoDB Sheets append mode from INSERT_ROWS to OVERWRITE to preserve pre-formatted cell styling, and adding an IF node ("Step 9-check") that routes duplicate records back into the loop instead of silently halting execution.
- Human approvers can only edit the Status and Edited Response columns — other columns are protected/locked ranges.
- **The daily summary email this workflow sends is explicitly documented as "internal operator-only"** — client-facing reporting is handled entirely by a separate MRA workflow. This is important context for one of the findings below.

